WEBVTT

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:31.720
<i>Suteta hazu no fuan no tane ga 
kokoro tsukiyabutte me o dashita</i>

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:47.950
<i>Musuu no ibara ga kyou mo 
ashimoto nobite machikamaeteiru</i>

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:56.410
<i>Doko e yukeba aeru</i>

00:00:56.410 --> 00:01:11.300
<i>Dakishimenaide senaka no toge 
wa kimi o kizutsukeru yo</i>

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:26.530
<i>Soredemo afureru omoi ga kimi o sagashiteiru</i>

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:36.030
"The Farthest Town"

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.890
We've arrived!

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.520
Ahh... It sure is a relief 
to be on solid ground.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:15.230
If we go a little further, we'll 
go into the system's range.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:17.990
Let's do a good chunk of 
maintenance here, shall we?

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:21.950
Yeah, we don't wanna have another 
problem with the system.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:23.200
Clain!

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.160
Yes, Sir!

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:31.960
Now, while they're working hard, 
let's prepare dinner, shall we?

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.830
Okay! Then, let's go, Phryne!

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:35.590
What?

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:47.560
About the next point...

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.730
the temple around here probably is... Hm?

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.450
Bro?

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:55.860
Come to think of it, that doppel...

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:57.480
Huh?

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:00.520
Why can we see her even 
when we're out of range?

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:08.910
Oh, geez... You're so clumsy.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:10.040
Let me do it!

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:11.330
No!

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:12.140
Huh?

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:16.460
Long... I'm peeling it so that the 
skin is long and doesn't get cut.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:20.260
You sure are particular over 
some silly things, aren't you?

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:23.180
Huh?

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:25.640
There! Take it!

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:28.410
Hey, Sanko! Is Nessa there, too?!

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:30.900
You two come and help us!

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:34.100
Come on, Phryne!

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:39.690
What?! Are you gonna swim, too?!

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:41.560
Ahh!

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:52.210
Oh? She's a bold one, isn't she?

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:56.170
Y-You know, you should get rid of that 
habit of taking off your clothes so easily!

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:59.610
Clain's naughty radar is super strong.

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:01.720
It'll go off soon and he'll be here in no...

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:01.720
Hey!

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:05.140
Everyone! Sunda wants you to come... What?!

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:09.140
He really came! He's naughty!

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:10.680
Naughty! Naughty!

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.560
No! I-It's not like that!

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:15.900
Ouch!

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.770
Naughty! Naughty!

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:20.610
Naughty! Naughty!

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:20.610
Stop it! It's cold!

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:23.420
Ah!

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:26.950
That's a camera!

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:29.190
He's sneaking photos!

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:31.270
Wait!

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:32.620
Clain!

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:37.500
Wait! Wait!

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:41.590
<i>Taking pictures using such 
an antique digital camera...</i>

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:43.130
<i>I can't believe it!</i>

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:45.930
To think that you can't forgive 
other's naughtiness...

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:48.470
Only naughty people would 
have that mentality.

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:53.280
Why did that man have a camera?

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:57.050
Are you still upset, Clain?

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:05.900
Where are those people going?

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:06.860
Beats me.

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.660
When they don't have anywhere to go...

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:09.990
What?

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:12.190
They're out-of-range refugees.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:13.670
Out-of-range refugees?

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:17.290
Yeah. They stopped being able to 
receive the benefits of Fractale

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:21.130
when the balloons fell and the 
radio waves stopped reaching them.

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:23.600
Since they were totally 
dependent on Fractale,

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:26.050
they can't live all by themselves.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:28.590
So they have no choice but 
to look for a new signal.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:31.030
Even though they got kicked out of Fractale,

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:33.930
all they can do is hold on 
to Fractale and wander about.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:35.770
They're pitiful nomads.

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:37.440
Oh no...

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:41.020
Nessa...

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:41.940
Stop it!

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:43.750
Don't touch it with your dirty hands!

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:44.690
I can't let you have this!

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:46.540
You've got food in it, right?!

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:48.030
Don't keep it all to yourself, pops!

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:49.700
Ah! That's...

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:53.160
Stealing isn't unusual among 
out-of-range refugees...

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:56.620
as they're completely unruly.

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:57.870
Oh no!

00:05:58.370 --> 00:05:59.250
Clain!

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:00.960
Stop it!

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:03.620
Stop it!

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:04.630
Who the hell are you?!

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:07.260
There's something valuable in this!

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:09.820
What're you doing, Clain?!

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:11.700
The refugees are irritated now.

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:12.510
You'll cause a...

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:24.530
Please calm down!

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:41.420
Who's this guy?

00:06:42.890 --> 00:06:44.210
Does that hurt?

00:06:45.230 --> 00:06:50.630
But this superficial pain isn't what 
you should really be bothered about...

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:53.050
Let me... Ow!

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:55.350
The pain you <i>should </i>be focusing on

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:59.350
is from the gaping hole left in your 
heart when Fractale betrayed you.

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:00.810
Dias...

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:04.770
I haven't seen you in a while, Sunda.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.360
You look as well as ever.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:10.610
Looks like you're the same as ever.

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:12.910
What?! You know him?

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:16.620
We're the Alabaster.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:21.120
Based in Kilda, we're acting as part 
of the Lost Millennium movement!

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:25.840
We'd like to help all of you 
who were betrayed by Fractale.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:28.220
One sector east from here,

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:30.470
there's a town forsaken by Fractale.

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:32.300
Let's go there.

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:35.800
We'll give you food as well as warm beds.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:39.700
Don't worry. Trust us.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:54.560
Are you okay?

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:57.830
He ran off.

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:00.250
After we went through the 
trouble of helping him...

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:02.370
This is why I say pervs are...

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:05.000
Huh? Ah, h-hey!

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:13.500
I wonder where he went...

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:25.100
Wow! This is such a primitive antenna!

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:26.440
What'd you come here for?

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:30.670
I-It's not what you think!

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:33.700
I didn't come to blame 
you for sneaking photos!

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:36.200
Well, sneaking photos is 
a bad thing to do, but...

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:39.740
Well, Phryne does take off her 
clothes without thinking anyway.

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:40.700
Er, no!

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.540
What'd you come here for?

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:43.620
Just answer that question.

00:08:44.030 --> 00:08:47.880
I... want to be your friend, Mister!

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:52.300
Wow!

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:54.800
Th-This is amazing! A gold mine!

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:57.990
Whoa! These are vacuum tubes!

00:08:57.990 --> 00:08:59.050
I've never seen them before!

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:02.030
This place is like a relic!

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:05.560
Are you interested in antiques?

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:06.310
Yes!

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:07.770
Why?

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:10.900
They're just wreckage from the 
past that are of no use anymore.

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:14.570
I wonder why... It started... yeah,

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:17.890
because there was a projector 
at home... maybe...

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:22.700
I think my parents probably left it...

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:24.160
but for some reason, I got hooked.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:27.120
But my parents' doppels 
make a big stink about it,

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:29.880
telling me to ditch stupid stuff.

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:32.460
Whoa! This cell phone is 
from the 21st century!

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:35.840
This is really cool...

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:39.720
Unlike data, it really exists here.

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:41.930
It feels like it's really alive.

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:44.350
That way of thinking... You must be from L.M.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:47.020
No! I'm not from L.M.!

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:48.520
Those terrorists...

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:54.890
But I also feel like... they're 
not really that bad...

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:57.650
You don't understand anything.

00:09:57.650 --> 00:09:58.360
Huh?

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:00.700
There's a new moon tonight, huh?

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:01.820
This is good timing.

00:10:01.820 --> 00:10:03.700
Come back here late at night.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:04.950
What?

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:07.810
I'll show you something very valuable.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:12.130
What?! We're out of soup already?!

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:15.760
Of course! You weren't here at dinnertime.

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:19.900
Rules are important when living 
together with others! You know, rules!

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:25.810
Oh yeah... I think I'm gonna 
go to those Alabaster people.

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:27.310
They said they'd be distributing food, so...

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:31.730
If you receive alms from the Alabaster, 
I'll kick you off of the Danan!

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:34.570
What?! They're part of the L.M., right?

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:36.320
Aren't they your friends?

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:40.160
There're all sorts of people 
in the L.M., you know.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:42.660
We do things smarter than them.

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:43.740
Smarter?!

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:49.210
Anyway you look at it, that Dias person 
seems more intelligent than Sunda.

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:53.920
Build up your strength by eating some 
hard leftover bread or something.

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:57.250
You get to stand watch all night tonight.

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:27.470
Where're you going?

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:30.060
P-Please let me go!

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:32.250
There's this place I absolutely wanna go.

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:34.500
Even when you have to skip on standing watch?

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:37.700
Yeah... Remember that man with a camera?

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:39.760
I made a promise with him.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:41.170
So it's Mr. Naughty, huh?

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:44.490
N-No! He isn't like that...

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:46.760
I think... I'm sure...

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:50.460
You have such an interest in him...

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:52.850
I wanna talk to him, too!

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:58.020
What?! You see, this is a man-to-man promise.

00:11:58.020 --> 00:12:00.870
I'm sorry to say this, 
but girls can't join us.

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:07.830
I am a person whose name is 
Phryne before I am a girl.

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:11.120
Did he tell you not to bring Phryne?

00:12:11.510 --> 00:12:14.960
Ah! Hey! Wait up!

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:24.470
Hm? That light...

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:26.640
That must be Alabaster.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:29.890
Hey, hey! Don't cut in line!

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:35.100
There's plenty more, so get in line!

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:38.940
We're now ready to perform vaccinations.

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:41.610
Those who were under Fractale's protection

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:44.740
are susceptible to the alpha virus.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:46.160
Is that free, too?

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:47.580
Of course.

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:51.870
To the L.M., both donay and 
monay are simply numbers.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:56.710
Oh, thanks. No one has 
been so kind to me before.

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:58.080
You're overreacting.

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:03.130
It's true! I'll be sure to repay 
you for your kindness, mister.

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:04.670
Now, please come in.

00:13:04.670 --> 00:13:05.880
Yeah!

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:12.640
Now, get in line!

00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:18.390
Wow... I guess there're all kinds 
of people in the L.M. as well.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:23.780
To think that they even perform 
vaccinations for epidemic diseases...

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:24.950
I'm a bit impressed.

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:29.070
I like everyone in the Granites better.

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:33.040
I-It's not like I'm badmouthing the Granites.

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.530
Well, they've got some problems,

00:13:35.530 --> 00:13:37.420
but they're not bad guys.

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:39.500
Are you saying that Alabaster 
doesn't have problems?

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:41.670
What? They don't, right?

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:44.520
You saw how happy those 
people with them looked.

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:52.890
What's with you?

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:54.310
What's with <i>you</i>?

00:13:58.400 --> 00:13:59.860
You hate to lose, don't you?

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:01.270
Same with you!

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:10.740
A girl?

00:14:11.230 --> 00:14:13.660
I... I'm sorry. Well...

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.780
Good evening, Mr. Naughty.

00:14:15.780 --> 00:14:17.350
I'm coming inside.

00:14:17.350 --> 00:14:19.420
Phryne! You shouldn't do 
that without permission!

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:22.040
Is she your girlfriend?

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:23.360
No!

00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:26.630
Okay. She can come, too.

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:28.800
Th-Thank you very much!

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:30.300
Phryne, hurry up!

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:32.640
Okay.

00:14:39.770 --> 00:14:42.900
<i>I know you said that you're 
Phryne before you're a girl...</i>

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:45.780
<i>but you should at least be 
aware that you're a girl.</i>

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:50.610
Wow! It looks even more amazing up close!

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:51.990
Just like the Danan,

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:53.990
this is a patchwork of all sorts of parts.

00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:58.080
Almost there...

00:14:58.080 --> 00:14:58.910
Huh?

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:00.790
In just a moment, I'll show you

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:02.960
something more amazing than any antiques.

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:22.400
On nights when there's a new moon, the 
temple interferes with the balloons.

00:15:22.780 --> 00:15:25.320
The radio waves temporarily strengthen.

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:28.280
This antenna picked them up.

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:29.560
I see...

00:15:29.560 --> 00:15:32.820
This is how this area looked 
before their balloon fell.

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:35.840
I want to put this area back within range.

00:15:35.840 --> 00:15:37.200
That's my wish.

00:15:38.820 --> 00:15:43.800
The people of this world can no 
longer live without Fractale.

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:47.460
So, instead of wandering about 
in search of radio waves,

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:52.700
we'll bring the benefits of 
Fractale to this place. That's...

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:55.510
Mister!

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:01.500
Not yet!

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:05.230
The real thing that I want 
to show you comes after this.

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:05.810
What?!

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:11.780
Go down to the town and see 
the truth with your own eyes.

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:13.560
The truth?

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:23.620
Oh, how beautiful...

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:24.960
This is Fractale's scenery.

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:26.920
What're you seeing?!

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:29.000
Don't play games! I can't see it!

00:16:29.600 --> 00:16:31.010
What happened?

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:37.510
What?! What happened to him?!

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:38.050
Clain!

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:39.920
No, Clain!

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:44.140
Look closely!

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:48.420
Ah! This is...

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:52.610
Mr. Dias...

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:54.880
Why did the radio waves...

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:57.570
We haven't finished the 
procedure on everyone yet.

00:16:57.940 --> 00:17:00.490
Hey, Mister. What's going on?

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:02.080
Oh, are you shocked?

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:04.910
The treatment that we 
gave you guys earlier...

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:08.210
That was a very simple surgery 
to remove your terminals.

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:09.420
What?!

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:10.420
Oh no...

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:12.130
Then we can never receive Fractale's...

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:14.150
Hey! What have you done?!

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:18.140
You'd be sure to repay us for our kindness...

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:19.390
If I recall correctly, that 
was what you said, wasn't it?

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:27.350
Then, let's fight together... 
fight Fractale together with us.

00:17:35.230 --> 00:17:36.320
I'm getting out of here!

00:17:36.850 --> 00:17:38.280
To where?

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:45.620
There's nowhere to escape.

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:48.100
Even if you get within range,

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:51.210
you can't receive Fractale's benefits...

00:17:51.210 --> 00:17:53.090
since you don't have terminals anymore.

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:57.550
Don't worry. We'll help you.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:02.640
Clain!

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:18.960
Clain...

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:25.120
Are you okay?

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:27.780
It's already gone back?

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:29.750
Mister!

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:34.220
This is the limit of that antenna...

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:36.840
but were you able to see the truth?

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:39.640
Y-Yes... I think...

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:42.140
More importantly, you should rest!

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:43.010
Oh yes.

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:45.890
We'll take you on the Danan to an area 
where Fractale's radio waves reach!

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:47.060
Let Fractale treat you.

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:48.690
No thanks.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:50.850
But... you'll die if you don't!

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:52.320
That's okay.

00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:57.030
Besides, even if I die, I 
doubt anyone will be sad.

00:18:57.330 --> 00:18:58.080
Ah...

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:03.990
I think I'll probably be sad.

00:19:04.340 --> 00:19:05.150
What?

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:08.640
Although I had friends with the same hobby,

00:19:08.640 --> 00:19:10.370
I've never actually met them.

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:12.610
I don't know their real faces...

00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:14.860
I've never talked with 
them in person like this.

00:19:16.310 --> 00:19:19.000
So...! So...

00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:21.060
Thank you...

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:25.260
But I can't abandon that house.

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:26.100
Why not?!

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:29.390
It's just like collecting antiques.

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:31.200
You were talking about it, too...

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:34.610
about the things that are alive, unlike data.

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:38.030
The precious memories that 
I left in the past...

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:42.820
It may seem silly, but I want 
to hold onto those things.

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:48.480
I want to keep looking for radio waves 
at this place where my memories remain.

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:52.580
Okay.

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:54.060
Clain...

00:19:57.090 --> 00:19:58.500
I'll give this to you.

00:19:58.810 --> 00:19:59.710
What?!

00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:00.970
Here.

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:06.930
Wow... Wh-Why are you giving it to me?

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:15.070
Clain...

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:32.580
Hm? Photos?

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:34.040
I stole them.

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:35.530
You stole them?!

00:20:35.530 --> 00:20:38.130
You may not look it, but you sure are...

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:40.380
Ah! These are the photos that guy took!

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:44.840
I see... He wasn't as naughty as I thought.

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:47.140
This one is quite old, though...

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:50.220
The baby's fingers are small!

00:20:51.720 --> 00:20:54.310
I know who this baby is.

00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:56.150
Really? Who is it?

00:21:24.810 --> 00:21:37.480
<i>Madoromi to fuyu no gogo 
kurikaesareru hibi mo</i>

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:51.930
<i>Yanagi o suberiochiru 
tada ichido kiri no yume</i>

00:21:52.660 --> 00:22:06.210
<i>Okizari no nukumori hikari ni kawaru made</i>

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:20.200
<i>Kayoinareta hidamari ni anata o utsushimasu</i>

00:22:34.410 --> 00:22:48.510
<i>Hoho o naderu hidamari ni anata o omoidasu</i>
